 the ellipse is centered at $(-4,0),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b93e18213fdd67fce8b8bd708b1fe0842a7aca3225235ce4308e7e1682a8a1a" "basis" 630 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115297" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f0e36ba8271e2e827a6c40d37f976e956cdd830dd7da7aeb4e083adaf36cf30e" "basis" 630 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b93e18213fdd67fce8b8bd708b1fe0842a7aca3225235ce4308e7e1682a8a1a" "basis" 630 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115297" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13958359/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b93e18213fdd67fce8b8bd708b1fe0842a7aca3225235ce4308e7e